        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py: prepare_checkout calls `env = github_git_env(source, Path(root))` for every non-local source. github_git_env raises WorkerError('harness git access requires an uncredentialed GitHub HTTPS origin') for any other scheme or host, and calls active_gh_token unconditionally. A public clone with no gh login, or an ssh or other-host source that cloned before, now fails. The added tests cover only the private and missing-token cases; none checks that a public reposi",
                  "id": "clone-requires-token-for-public-github",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "prepare_checkout and prepare_harness now require a gh credential for every GitHub HTTPS source, public ones included. They also reject any non-GitHub or non-file remote. The spec only requires the credential for a private repository, and the tasks claim public behaviour is unchanged."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "scripts/live_scenarios.py close_open_work: `gh_json([\"api\", \"--paginate\", f\"repos/{repo}/branches?per_page=100\"], SOURCE_ROOT)`, where gh_json is `json.loads(run(...))`. The code adds no `--slurp` and does no per-page handling.",
                  "id": "close-open-work-paginate-json",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "close_open_work parses `gh api --paginate` output with json.loads. For a repository with more than 100 branches, gh prints one JSON array per page, so the concatenated output is not valid JSON and reset would crash. Leftover work branches build up across failed runs."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "scripts/live_scenarios.py Lock.acquire does `DELETE` then `_create()` without comparing the holder value before the delete. Sandbox.env sets `env[\"GH_TOKEN\"] = run([\"gh\",\"auth\",\"token\"], ...)`, and Scenario.platform and finish_until_queued pass that env to scripts executed from sandbox.checkout.",
                  "id": "lock-takeover-race-and-operator-token",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "Two minor robustness gaps in the runner. First, the expired-lock takeover is not atomic: two runners that both see an expired lease can each delete the other's freshly created variable, and both then believe they hold the lock. Second, the operator's full gh login token is exported as GH_TOKEN to ev"
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "f9e8b72f8fcbf2cfec6abb899e97feb30ca32ca53daab339d939a69bca4d16bc"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "tasks.md 2.2 says 'Idempotent bootstrap of the repository, settings, protection and labels; target guard.' In scripts/live_scenarios.py, `Sandbox.apply_settings` covers merge settings, the HOSTED_KINDS variable, branch protection and a ruleset. `check_target` fails if the repository does not exist. Nothing creates labels (grep the diff for 'label'). docs/engineering/live-scenarios.md lists the repository and labels in neither the owner setup nor the runner steps.",
                  "id": "bootstrap-repo-and-labels-not-implemented",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "Task 2.2 is marked done as an idempotent bootstrap of the repository, settings, protection and labels. The runner only does settings, protection and a ruleset. It does not create the repository or any labels."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "specs/publication-queue/spec.md: 'grant the coordinator token of each queue workflow it installs Checks read and Actions read'. sandbox.toml has kept_workflows = [publication-queue.yml, lifecycle-workers.yml], and compose_snapshot calls grant_token_reads on every kept workflow. design.md and docs say 'snapshot workflows'. The delta spec should name the worker workflow too, or the runner should not touch it.",
                  "id": "token-read-grant-scope-wider-than-spec",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The spec limits the Checks and Actions read grant to the queue workflows. The runner applies it to every kept workflow, including lifecycle-workers.yml."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "spec-fidelity",
              "report_sha256": "3d30b56af7bd3fb754694642722fc6d3fcc8814a079c70ea5c8dd9efdeea63a5"
            }
          },
